WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.440
- [Narrator] For over 200 million years

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.400
these creatures have roamed the Earth,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.160
but now their future is uncertain.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.583
This is the American horseshoe crab.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.120
Found along the Atlantic
coastline of North America,

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.260
the American horseshoe crab
spends the majority of its time

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.800
in shallow waters but
comes to shore to mate.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.650
The crab has 10 eyes,
the two most obvious ones

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.070
are on the top of its shell

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.653
but the others are on the
tail and near the mouth.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.500
Horseshoe crabs are
harvested for their blood

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.530
which has helped prevent
illnesses across the globe;

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.800
but with the development
of their natural habitat

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.630
and over-harvesting,
this once abundant animal

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.230
has now seen such a
rapid decline in numbers

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.763
that they are considered
a vulnerable species.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.983
This is the American horseshoe crab.

